Day 21: Setting Up an EC2 Instance with an Elastic IP for Application Hosting

The instance will be named xfusion-ec2, and the Elastic IP will be named xfusion-eip. 
This setup will help the Development Team to have a reliable and consistent access point for their application.
Create an EC2 instance named xfusion-ec2 using any linux AMI like ubuntu
The Instance type must be t2.micro 
Associate an Elastic IP address with this instance, name it as xfusion-eip.

1. Check AMI ID
aws-client ~ ➜  aws ec2 describe-images --owners 099720109477 \
--filters "Name=name,Values=ubuntu/images/hvm-ssd/ubuntu-jammy-22.04-amd64-server-*" \
--query 'sort_by(Images, &CreationDate)[-1].ImageId' --output text
ami-0ff290337e78c83bf

2. Create keypair
aws-client ~ ✖  aws ec2 create-key-pair --key-name myKeyPair --query 'KeyMaterial' --output text > myKeyPair.pem
aws-client ~ ➜  chmod 400 myKeyPair.pem 

